**[LESSON]: Can't model direct assignment as a factless predicate referencing a variable relation → Must introduce an explicit directAssignment relation or otherwise abstract its use in holdsRoleDirectly.**
**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 requires explicit signatures for relations—predicates cannot declare/define relations on the fly.**
**[LESSON]: No "if-then-else" expressions in Alloy 6 → Use implications or explicit set comprehensions.**
**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 set comprehensions must have explicit variable bindings and cannot use "let" to bind relation projections directly—must use let to bind values.**
**[LESSON]: To enforce symmetry and pairing of mutex roles, must introduce a signature capturing both directions and require the symmetric pair to exist.**
**[LESSON]: Model coverage/witness properties with predicates, not facts, to avoid overconstraining the system.**
**[LESSON]: Avoid using facts for properties that must be checked incrementally or via predicates; facts always hold, so will block instances if overconstrained.**
**[LESSON]: Alloy 6 type system: set union (+) works on compatible sets, and set intersection (&) is for overlapping sets.**
**[LESSON]: Run predicates for witness/coverage, and check assertions for safety/invariant properties.**

