Classification: spec_clarification: Results reveal either a requirement ambiguity or a hidden conflict concerning the coexistence of active delegations in both Emergency and Normal modes and the semantics/timing of emergency privilege assignment/revocation.
Rationale: The persistent UNSAT on DelegationCoverageEmergency and DelegationCoverage, together with assertion failures, despite model adjustments and passing incremental requirements, points to a requirement ambiguity or contradiction rather than a pure modeling error.

=== BLOCKING QUESTIONS ===
1. Is it permissible for different delegation instances to be active in Emergency mode and in Normal mode (i.e., must there always exist at least one delegation in each mode, but not necessarily the same delegation instance persisting across both modes), or is the requirement that at least one such instance exists for each mode, even if no delegation ever persists across the Emergency/Normal transition?
