[DelegationCoverageEmergency, DelegationCoverage]

DelegationCoverageEmergency requires: 
- Existence of at least one State in EmergencyMode with some active Delegation where: 
  • d.duringEmergency = True 
  • d.revoked = False 
  • d.delegatedAt ≤ sE.t < d.expiresAt (or no expiresAt)

DelegationCoverage requires this for both Emergency and Normal modes (distinct delegations, not cross-mode persistence).

Key atomic constraints:
- All Emergency-mode delegations are revoked at Emergency/Normal transition (EmergencyDelegationAndPrivilegeRevocation fact).
- Roles delegated during Emergency must have d.duringEmergency = True.
- Delegations delegated before Emergency (d.duringEmergency = False) persist unless expired/revoked.

Blocking points:
- At Emergency/Normal transition, all Emergency-mode delegations are revoked before the first NormalMode state.
- The requirement for at least one Emergency-mode delegation to exist at some EmergencyMode state, and at least one Normal-mode delegation at some NormalMode state, is possible only if delegations are created in each mode but not required to persist across the transition.
- If the only delegation created is during Emergency and it is revoked before first Normal mode state, and no new Normal-mode delegation is created after Emergency ends, the Normal-mode witness fails.
- If only Normal-mode delegations exist, the Emergency-mode witness fails.

