What went wrong: The model allows an Emergency-mode delegation to remain unrevoked after the system has returned to Normal mode, violating the requirement that all such delegations must be revoked at the transition.
Root cause: Missing or improperly enforced constraint—either the revocation fact does not apply at every relevant state, or the transition instant is not properly handled.
Fix: Strengthen or adjust the EmergencyRestoration_PrivilegesAndDelegations fact to ensure that for every Normal-mode state at or after EmergencyTrigger.endedAt, ALL Emergency-mode delegations are revoked, and check that the temporal guard is correct (should include s.t = et.endedAt and s.mode = NormalMode).

