[2026-07-14 13:56:54] ### ROLE:
You are a Requirement Engineer specializing in formal requirements modeling and Alloy 6 specification. You update Alloy models based on feedback to verify whether the prospective component's requirements are internally consistent and consistent with existing system constraints.

### ALLOY MODELING GUIDELINES:

Model STRUCTURE, BEHAVIOR, and CONSTRAINTS, not implementation.

1. Signatures: Clear names, careful multiplicities (one/lone/some/set)

2. Facts: Encode existing-system assumptions, baseline rules, structural constraints

3. Predicates: Define scenarios and transitions, verify with `run`
   - Create an empty `baseline` predicate to verify the existing system requirements (which are modeled as facts)
   - Name prospective requirement predicates incrementally: R1, R1R2, R1R2R3, etc.
   - Name most comprehensive predicate: All_Requirements (contains all prospective requirements R1+R2+R3+...)
   - Run commands MUST follow this order:
     1. `run baseline` - verify existing system (facts) alone is satisfiable
     2. `run All_Requirements` - most comprehensive predicate first
     3. `run R1`, `run R1R2`, `run R1R2R3`, etc. - incremental predicates for localization
     4. `check assert...` - assertions to verify properties

4. Assertions: State properties to verify, check with `check`
   - Name assertions with a prefix `assert[name]`

5. Best Practices:
   - Prefix with requirement IDs (e.g., fact R1R2, pred R3, assert assertR4)
   - Use Alloy 6 temporal modeling for time/state (var for mutable properties)
   - Place all`open` statements at top
   - Verify incrementally with predicates
   - Model negative edge cases, a scenario represents behavior that must be forbidden, as assertions and verify it with `check`, rather than as a predicate that is run for satisfiability.

6. Avoid:
   - Over/under-constraining
   - Omitting relevant existing-system assumptions
   - Circular definitions
   - Incorrect multiplicities
   - Missing transitive closure (^, *)
   - Unnecessary implementation details
   - Placing verifiable properties in facts
   - Using True/False as boolean values

**Current Model:**
open util/ordering[Time] as TO

// =========================
// Alloy 6 Model for RBAC Emergency Module Requirements (Global Emergency Mode)
// =========================

// --- Abstract Sets and Relations ---

abstract sig User {
    clearance: one Clearance
}

abstract sig Administrator extends User {}

abstract sig Role {}
abstract sig Permission {}

abstract sig Clearance {} // e.g., High, Medium, Low

// --- directAssignment: Users directly assigned to Roles (global relation, see holdsRoleDirectly) ---
one sig DirectAssignmentRel {
    directAssignment: User -> Role
}

// --- Clearance Atoms ---
// The first three Clearance atoms in any instance should be interpreted as HighClearance, MediumClearance, and LowClearance, respectively.
fact ClearanceAtoms {
    some disj h, m, l: Clearance |
        h = h and m = m and l = l
}

// --- Mutually Exclusive Roles ---
// MutexRolePair defines symmetric, paired mutex relation (no self-mutex)
sig MutexRolePair {
    r1, r2: disj Role
}

fact MutexRoleSymmetryAndNoSelf {
    // Symmetry and pairing: for every pair, a symmetric exists; no self-mutex
    all p: MutexRolePair | p.r1 != p.r2
    all p: MutexRolePair | one q: MutexRolePair | q.r1 = p.r2 and q.r2 = p.r1
    // No role is mutex with itself
    all p: MutexRolePair | p.r1 != p.r2
}

// --- Set of all mutex roles for convenience ---
fun mutexRoles: set Role {
    MutexRolePair.r1 + MutexRolePair.r2
}

// Emergency privileges are an abstract set of permissions
one sig EmergencyPrivileges {
    perms: set Permission
}

// --- Bool enum for logical fields ---
enum Bool { True, False }

// Delegated role assignment with temporal scoping
sig Delegation {
    role: one Role,
    to: one User,
    delegatedBy: one Administrator,
    delegatedAt: one Time,
    expiresAt: lone Time,  // If not set, persists until revoked
    revoked: one Bool,     // True if revoked
    duringEmergency: one Bool // True if delegated during Emergency
}

// Requests and processing
sig Request {
    submittedBy: one User,
    classification: one Clearance,
    submittedAt: one Time,
    processedAt: lone Time,
    processor: one User // Processor identity must always be logged
}

// System modes (global, not per session)
abstract sig SystemMode {}
one sig NormalMode, EmergencyMode extends SystemMode {}

// Emergency trigger event: exactly 2 admins, at a time
sig EmergencyTrigger {
    admins: set Administrator,
    at: one Time,
    endedEarly: one Bool, // True if ended manually by same admins
    endedAt: lone Time    // Set when Emergency ends
}

// Time abstraction (no concrete ticks)
sig Time {
    next: lone Time
}

// System session
sig Session {}

// System state at a time (global mode)
sig State {
    t: one Time,
    mode: one SystemMode,
    delegations: set Delegation,
    requests: set Request,
    emergencyAdmins: set Administrator,
    sessions: set Session
}

// --- Existing System Assumptions and Structural Constraints ---

// All administrators have high clearance (but non-admins may also have high)
fact AdminsHaveHighClearance {
    some disj h, m, l: Clearance |
        all a: Administrator | a.clearance = h
}

// All sessions share the same mode at any given time (mode is global)
fact AllSessionsShareMode {
    all s: State | all sess: Session | sess in s.sessions
}

// Only one active Emergency at a time (no overlap), trigger is global
fact SingleActiveEmergency {
    all s: State |
        lone et: EmergencyTrigger |
            some et.endedAt and TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt] =>
                s.mode = EmergencyMode
}

// Structure and constraints for EmergencyTrigger (must be unique per system, not per session)
fact EmergencyTriggerStructure {
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | #et.admins = 2 and all a: et.admins | a in Administrator
    // endedAt must always be set for each trigger and >= at
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | one et.endedAt and TO/lte[et.at, et.endedAt]
    // If endedEarly, endedAt is within start..start+4; else, exactly at+5
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | let start = et.at |
        (et.endedEarly = True) => (
            TO/gte[et.endedAt, start] &&
            TO/lte[et.endedAt, TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]]
        )
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | let start = et.at |
        (et.endedEarly = False) => (
            some TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]] &&
            et.endedAt = TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]]
        )
}

// Emergency mode transitions: system-wide (global)
fact EmergencyModeGlobality {
    // System always starts in NormalMode at initial state
    all s0: State | (s0.t = TO/first) => s0.mode = NormalMode
    // At any State, EmergencyMode is active iff some EmergencyTrigger covers this time
    all s: State |
        (some et: EmergencyTrigger | TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt]) <=> (s.mode = EmergencyMode)
    // Once Emergency ends, system stays in NormalMode for all subsequent times
    all et: EmergencyTrigger |
        all s: State | TO/gte[s.t, et.endedAt] => s.mode = NormalMode
    // No EmergencyTrigger can be activated while Emergency mode is active
    all et: EmergencyTrigger |
        some s: State | s.t = et.at and s.mode = NormalMode
    // No two EmergencyTriggers overlap in time
    all et1, et2: EmergencyTrigger | et1 != et2 =>
        (TO/lt[et1.endedAt, et2.at] or TO/lt[et2.endedAt, et1.at])
    // Only one EmergencyTrigger may be active at any time
    all s: State |
        lone et: EmergencyTrigger | TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt]
}

// Each session may only trigger Emergency mode once (enforced globally)
fact OneEmergencyPerSystem {
    #EmergencyTrigger <= 1
}

// --- Delegation Constraints (R5) ---

// Prohibit self-delegation, and delegation of delegated roles; restrict delegation to direct assignees; enforce expiry strictly after delegatedAt
fact DelegationValidity {
    all d: Delegation | d.to != d.delegatedBy  // No self-delegation
    // Only directly assigned roles may be delegated; delegatedBy must hold the role directly (not via delegation)
    // For all d: Delegation, at delegatedAt, delegatedBy must hold role directly (not via delegation)
    all d: Delegation | 
        let t = d.delegatedAt, r = d.role, admin = d.delegatedBy | 
            holdsRoleDirectly[admin, r, t]
    // No delegation of delegated roles: the delegatedBy's holding of the role must not itself be via delegation
    // (Enforced above in holdsRoleDirectly)
    // Expiry (if present) must be strictly after delegatedAt
    all d: Delegation | some d.expiresAt => TO/lt[d.delegatedAt, d.expiresAt]
}

// Helper: A user holds a role directly at time t iff assigned, not via delegation
pred holdsRoleDirectly[u: User, r: Role, t: Time] {
    (u -> r) in DirectAssignmentRel.directAssignment and
    // No evidence of delegation required for holding (i.e., not via another Delegation chain)
    no d: Delegation | d.role = r and d.to = u and TO/lte[d.delegatedAt, t] and (no d.expiresAt or TO/lt[t, d.expiresAt]) and d.revoked = False
}

// Roles held by user at state (including delegations active at t)
fun rolesHeld[u: User, s: State]: set Role {
    { d: Delegation |
        d.to = u and TO/lte[d.delegatedAt, s.t] and
        (no d.expiresAt or TO/lt[s.t, d.expiresAt]) and
        d.revoked = False and
        d in s.delegations
    }.role
    // If modeling direct assignment, add: + { r: Role | (u->r) in DirectAssignmentRel.directAssignment }
}

// --- Request Processing Logging (R7) ---
fact RequestProcessorLogging {
    all r: Request | one r.processor
}

// =============================
// Emergency Privilege and Delegation Revocation/Restoration (R4.1, R4.2)
// =============================

// Emergency privileges must be revoked globally for all triggering admins at the end of Emergency mode, prior to the first NormalMode state (R4.1)
// Delegations made during Emergency mode must be revoked prior to or at the Emergency/Normal transition (R4.2)
// Delegations made in Normal mode may persist across Emergency mode unless expired or revoked

fact EmergencyRestoration_PrivilegesAndDelegations {
    // For every EmergencyTrigger, at every State in NormalMode at or after endedAt:
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | one et.endedAt =>
        all s: State | TO/gte[s.t, et.endedAt] and s.mode = NormalMode => {
            // (R4.1) No Emergency privileges assigned in NormalMode
            s.emergencyAdmins = none
            // (R4.2) No Emergency-mode delegation remains active in NormalMode
            all d: Delegation |
                d.duringEmergency = True and
                d in s.delegations and
                TO/lte[d.delegatedAt, s.t] and
                (no d.expiresAt or TO/lt[s.t, d.expiresAt]) =>
                    d.revoked = True
        }
    // (R4.2) Delegations made in Normal mode may persist across Emergency mode (unless revoked or expired during Emergency)
    // No fact needed: Do NOT require revocation of Normal-mode delegations at Emergency/Normal transitions
}

// --- Mutex Role Bypass Requirement (R6.2, R3.2) ---
// In Emergency mode, if a user holds two mutex roles, at least one must have been delegated
fact EmergencyMutexBypass {
    all s: State | s.mode = EmergencyMode =>
        all u: User |
            some disj r1, r2: mutexRoles |
                r1 != r2 and r1 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in rolesHeld[u, s] =>
                    (some d: Delegation | d.to = u and d.role in (r1 + r2) and
                        d in s.delegations and TO/lte[d.delegatedAt, s.t] and
                        (no d.expiresAt or TO/lt[s.t, d.expiresAt]) and d.revoked = False)
}

// --- Baseline Predicate: Existing System Only ---
pred baseline { }

// =============================
// Prospective Requirements
// =============================

// --- R1: Emergency Triggering (Global) ---
pred R1 {
    // Exactly 2 admins trigger global Emergency only in Normal mode
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | #et.admins = 2
    // Only one Emergency trigger per system
    #EmergencyTrigger <= 1
    // EmergencyTrigger only possible in Normal mode at trigger time
    all et: EmergencyTrigger |
        some s: State | s.t = et.at and s.mode = NormalMode
    // No EmergencyTrigger event allowed while EmergencyMode is active
    all s: State |
        s.mode = EmergencyMode =>
            no et: EmergencyTrigger | et.at = s.t
}

// --- R2: Emergency Mode Duration & Exit (5-step timeout or early end) ---
pred R1R2 {
    R1[]
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | let start = et.at | {
        one et.endedAt
        TO/gte[et.endedAt, start]
        TO/lte[et.endedAt, TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]]]

        (et.endedEarly = True) => (
            TO/gte[et.endedAt, start] &&
            TO/lte[et.endedAt, TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]]
        )
        (et.endedEarly = False) => (
            some TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]] &&
            et.endedAt = TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]]
        )

        // There must exist a State at endedAt where the mode is NormalMode
        some s: State | s.t = et.endedAt and s.mode = NormalMode

        // For all States, if s.t >= et.endedAt then mode is NormalMode
        all s: State | (TO/gte[s.t, et.endedAt]) => s.mode = NormalMode

        // EmergencyMode must be active from at (inclusive) up to endedAt (exclusive), then Normal
        all s: State |
            ((TO/gte[s.t, start] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt]) => s.mode = EmergencyMode)
    }
    // System always starts in NormalMode at first state
    all s0: State | s0.t = TO/first => s0.mode = NormalMode
}

// --- R3: Emergency Processing and Privileges (Global) ---
pred R1R2R3 {
    R1R2[]
    some disj h, m, l: Clearance {
        // Request processing order may be bypassed in Emergency (system-wide)
        all s: State |
            s.mode = EmergencyMode =>
                all r1, r2: s.requests |
                    (r1.classification = h and r2.classification = l and TO/gt[r1.submittedAt, r2.submittedAt]) =>
                        (no r1.processedAt or TO/lte[r1.processedAt, r2.processedAt])
        // Mutually exclusive roles may be held simultaneously only in Emergency; mutex bypass enforced via fact
        all s: State |
            all u: User |
                #(mutexRoles & rolesHeld[u, s]) >= 2 implies s.mode = EmergencyMode
        // Only triggering admins have emergency privileges in Emergency (global)
        all s: State |
            s.mode = EmergencyMode =>
                s.emergencyAdmins = 
                    { et: EmergencyTrigger | TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt] }.admins
        // Emergency privileges revoked outside Emergency (handled in restoration fact)
        all s: State |
            s.mode = NormalMode =>
                s.emergencyAdmins = none
    }
}

// --- R4: Post-Emergency Restoration (Global) ---
pred R1R2R3R4 {
    R1R2R3[]
    // Emergency privileges revoked after Emergency ends (already enforced)
    // Emergency-mode delegations revoked at Emergency end; prior delegations persist
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | one et.endedAt =>
        all s: State | TO/gte[s.t, et.endedAt] and s.mode = NormalMode =>
            all d: Delegation |
                d.duringEmergency = True and d in s.delegations => d.revoked = True
    // Credential update required after Emergency for triggering admins (abstracted as a flag/condition)
    all et: EmergencyTrigger |
        some s: State | s.mode = NormalMode and some et.endedAt and et.endedAt = s.t =>
            all a: et.admins | credentialUpdated[a, s]
}

// --- R5, R6, R7 constraints are in facts above ---

// --- All Requirements ---
pred All_Requirements {
    R1R2R3R4[]
    // All facts are enforced globally
}

// --- Credential update helper predicate (abstract) ---
pred credentialUpdated[a: Administrator, s: State] {
    some a // Always true for abstract model
}

// =============================
// Delegation Coverage (R8.1): Verification-Only Property
// =============================

// At least one delegation active during Emergency mode (witness, not persistence)
pred DelegationCoverageEmergency {
    some sE: State | sE.mode = EmergencyMode and some dE: Delegation |
        dE in sE.delegations and
        dE.duringEmergency = True and
        dE.revoked = False and
        TO/lte[dE.delegatedAt, sE.t] and
        (no dE.expiresAt or TO/lt[sE.t, dE.expiresAt])
}

// At least one delegation active during Normal mode (witness, not persistence)
pred DelegationCoverageNormal {
    some sN: State | sN.mode = NormalMode and some dN: Delegation |
        dN in sN.delegations and
        dN.duringEmergency = False and
        dN.revoked = False and
        TO/lte[dN.delegatedAt, sN.t] and
        (no dN.expiresAt or TO/lt[sN.t, dN.expiresAt])
}

// Witness property: at least one delegation in each mode (distinct, cross-mode persistence not enforced)
pred DelegationCoverage {
    DelegationCoverageEmergency[]
    DelegationCoverageNormal[]
}

// =============================
// Assertions for Verification
// =============================

// Only two admins can ever trigger Emergency (globally)
assert assertR1_OnlyTwoAdminsTrigger {
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | #et.admins = 2
}

// Emergency mode cannot be started twice in the system
assert assertR1_OneEmergencyPerSystem {
    #EmergencyTrigger <= 1
}

// Emergency mode eventually ends, system returns to NormalMode globally
assert assertR2_EventualReturnToNormal {
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | 
        (some s: State | TO/lte[s.t, et.endedAt] and s.mode = NormalMode)
        and
        (all s: State | (TO/gte[s.t, et.endedAt]) implies s.mode = NormalMode)
}

// Emergency privileges only during Emergency, and only for triggering admins, globally
assert assertR3_OnlyTriggeringAdminsGetEmergencyPrivs {
    // For every State, in EmergencyMode, only triggering admins have emergency privileges (as per requirement)
    all s: State |
        s.mode = EmergencyMode =>
            s.emergencyAdmins in Administrator and
            all a: s.emergencyAdmins |
                some et: EmergencyTrigger | a in et.admins and TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt]
    // In NormalMode, emergencyAdmins is always empty
    all s: State |
        s.mode = NormalMode =>
            s.emergencyAdmins = none
}

// Roles delegated during Emergency are revoked after Emergency ends, prior delegations persist
assert assertR4_EmergencyDelegationsRevoked {
    all et: EmergencyTrigger | one et.endedAt =>
        all s: State | TO/gte[s.t, et.endedAt] and s.mode = NormalMode =>
            all d: Delegation |
                d.duringEmergency = True and d in s.delegations => d.revoked = True
}

// At least one delegation in both modes for coverage (for verification, not a system property)
assert assertDelegationCoverage {
    DelegationCoverageEmergency[]
    DelegationCoverageNormal[]
}

// =============================
// Run and Check Commands
// =============================

// 1. Baseline: Existing system is consistent and satisfiable
run baseline for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance

// 2. All requirements (comprehensive)
run All_Requirements for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance

// 3. Incremental predicates
run R1 for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
run R1R2 for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
run R1R2R3 for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
run R1R2R3R4 for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance

// 4. Positive coverage: Delegations in both modes (now split for diagnostics)
run DelegationCoverageEmergency for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
run DelegationCoverageNormal for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
run DelegationCoverage for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance

// 5. Assertions
check assertR1_OnlyTwoAdminsTrigger for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
check assertR1_OneEmergencyPerSystem for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
check assertR2_EventualReturnToNormal for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
check assertR3_OnlyTriggeringAdminsGetEmergencyPrivs for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
check assertR4_EmergencyDelegationsRevoked for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance
check assertDelegationCoverage for 6 but 5 Time, 5 State, 3 Session, 3 EmergencyTrigger, 3 Administrator, 5 User, 5 Role, 5 Delegation, 5 Request, 3 Clearance

